{
  "id": "COMPOUND:29839 - PROTEIN:5849",
  "verbalization": "Pseudopterosin Q appears to have multiple targets that ultimately lead to A549 cells, suggesting a potential role in modulating cellular processes within this cancer cell line. The evidence indicates that Pseudopterosin Q interacts with Thioredoxin, a protein involved in redox regulation and cellular stress response, which is then targeted by (Salicylato-O1,O2)silver and 5-Hydroxy-2-Methylchromone-7-O-Rutinoside. These compounds, in turn, have a target relationship with A549, implying a cascade of molecular interactions that could influence cell behavior. The presence of multiple targets, including both enzymatic and non-enzymatic pathways, suggests a complex mechanism by which Pseudopterosin Q may exert its effects on A549 cells. The integration of these pathways highlights the potential for Pseudopterosin Q to modulate cellular processes through redox regulation and stress response, potentially contributing to its biological activity in this context.",
